div.p:
—Cadieux’s use of “non-negotiable” was privately conveyed to Laird, and is not
                    necessarily the last word. If we make a major
                    issue of it now, the Canadian position undoubtedly will stiffen;

—the line proposed by State contains a veiled threat that unless the Canadians
                    change their position we may take some troops out of Europe. Once this becomes
                    known, as it will, all the Europeans will shudder;
